hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16766","He said: Waki narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Yahya ibn Husayn, from his mother, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) address in the Farewell Hajj saying: O people, fear Allah and hear and obey, even if a mutilated Abyssinian slave is appointed over you, so long as he upholds among you the Book of Allah, mighty and majestic."
